---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Hikmet Cakir: About Me">
  <section class="about-section">

    <div class="about-card">

      <div class="about-intro">
        <h1>About Me </h1>
        <div class="about-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/hikmet-cakir" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="GitHub">
            <i class="bi bi-github"></i>
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hikmetcakir/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="LinkedIn">
            <i class="bi bi-linkedin"></i>
          </a>
          <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/19926019/hikmet-cakir" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Stack Overflow">
            <i class="bi bi-stack-overflow"></i>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I'm a software engineer with experience building backend systems in high-stakes environments — banking, telecom, and enterprise platforms where reliability isn't optional.
        </p>
        <p>
          Right now I'm at Yapı Kredi Teknoloji, working on core banking infrastructure. That means collection systems, counter operations, DBS — the kind of software that processes real transactions every day and simply cannot fail. I ship new features into this environment and fix the deep, tricky bugs that surface in production-critical financial systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before this, I spent nearly three years at ING Bank modernizing legacy systems — migrating C++ and PL/SQL codebases into modern Java microservices, and building out non-financial risk tooling that integrated with the bank's internal frontend stack. Before that, at Huawei, I worked on a cloud-based multimedia messaging platform and helped adapt a large enterprise system for global markets.
        </p>
        <p>
          My stack is Java and Spring Boot at the core, with Oracle, PostgreSQL, Kafka, Elasticsearch, Docker, and OpenShift in the mix depending on the project. I hold two Oracle Java SE 8 certifications and take test coverage seriously — not as a box to check, but because I've seen what happens when you don't in a banking context.
        </p>
        <p>
          This blog is where I write about the things I find interesting or useful — design patterns, backend architecture, Spring internals, and occasionally the hard lessons from working on systems that serve real users at scale. If something here saves you an hour of debugging, that's a good day.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-section {
    padding: 3rem 15%;
  }

  .about-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 0.5px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .about-intro h1 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111;
    margin: 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .about-links a {
    color: #6b7280;
    font-size: 22px;
    transition: color 0.15s;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .about-links a:hover { color: #111; }

  .about-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }

  .about-body p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: #374151;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .about-section {
      padding: 3rem 5%;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-section {
      padding: 2rem 4%;
    }
    .about-card {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
    .about-intro h1 {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .about-section {
      padding: 1.5rem 16px 2rem;
    }
    .about-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }
    .about-intro {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
